# Spark DS — Figma MCP

Spark DS in Figma is the design source. Use Figma MCP tools to read designs and keep Figma aligned with code.

## Spark Figma file

| Field | Value |
|-------|-------|
| File | [Spark DS](https://www.figma.com/design/KYq9ka9Hg16HdfzR4gMoMH/Spark---DS) |
| `fileKey` | `KYq9ka9Hg16HdfzR4gMoMH` |
| Default `nodeId` | `620:10020` (use node from the URL the user shares when implementing a specific screen or component) |

Always pass `fileKey: "KYq9ka9Hg16HdfzR4gMoMH"` to Spark DS Figma MCP calls unless the user links a different file.

## Source priority

| Layer | Role |
|-------|------|
| Figma | Layout, variants, visual intent, variables in the library |
| `css/tokens.css` | Canonical token names and values in React/CSS |
| HTML docs | Usage guidelines, a11y, React prop API |

When Figma and `tokens.css` disagree, implement with `tokens.css` and flag the drift. Do not hardcode values from Figma that lack a token mapping.

## Design-to-code (Figma → React)

Use when implementing UI from a design or Figma link.

1. Parse `fileKey` and `nodeId` from the Figma URL (`620-10020` → `620:10020`).
2. Call **`get_design_context`** with `fileKey`, `nodeId`, `clientLanguages: "typescript"`, `clientFrameworks: "react"`.
3. Call **`search_design_system`** with the same `fileKey` to find Spark components and variables (Button, colors, spacing).
4. Read the matching page in this repo (`button.html`, foundations).
5. Grep `css/tokens.css` for token names. Map Figma variables to `--semantic-*` / `--semantic-button-*`.
6. Adapt MCP output to Spark React patterns (see `spark-ds-react-components.mdc`). MCP code is reference only, not final code.
7. Prefer Code Connect snippets when **`get_code_connect_map`** returns a mapping.

## Code-to-design (React → Figma)

Use when updating Figma to match code or building library assets.

1. Load **`figma-use`** skill before every **`use_figma`** call.
2. For full pages or screens, also load **`figma-generate-design`**.
3. For new components or variables, also load **`figma-generate-library`**.
4. Call **`search_design_system`** first. Reuse existing Spark components and variables; do not recreate from scratch.
5. Bind fills, text, spacing, and radii to Spark variables, not raw hex.
6. Work in small **`use_figma`** steps. Return created node IDs from each call.

## Useful MCP tools

| Tool | When |
|------|------|
| `get_design_context` | Primary design-to-code read for a frame or component |
| `get_screenshot` | Visual check without full code context |
| `get_metadata` | File structure, node names, IDs |
| `get_variable_defs` | Figma variable names and values at a node |
| `search_design_system` | Find Spark Button, tokens, styles by query |
| `get_code_connect_map` | Figma component → codebase mapping |
| `use_figma` | Create or edit nodes (requires `figma-use` skill) |

## Do not

- Implement from screenshot alone when `get_design_context` is available.
- Paste Tailwind or arbitrary hex from MCP output without mapping to Spark tokens.
- Call `use_figma` without loading the `figma-use` skill first.
- Invent component variants that are not in Figma or `button.html`.
